# The published page is compared byte for byte by the CI drift guard, and it is rendered from
# these aggregates. The build and the export both write LF explicitly so a rebuild matches on
# any OS; without these lines a Windows checkout converts the committed copies to CRLF, and
# every local rebuild then reports a stale page for a reason no commit caused.
docs/index.html text eol=lf
docs/data/*.json text eol=lf
# Generated the same way, by the same command, and diffed by the same guard: the valuation
# form's stylesheet and the bounds it validates against.
docs/app/styles.css text eol=lf
docs/app/config.json text eol=lf
# The hand-written half of the form, pinned for the same reason: a Windows checkout otherwise
# holds CRLF while the committed blob (and therefore the published page) holds LF, so any
# byte-level comparison against the live site reports a difference no commit caused.
docs/app/*.html text eol=lf
docs/app/*.js text eol=lf
# Not diffed by CI — regenerating them needs the artifact and the dataset — but they are read
# by the parity test on Linux, and the exported model is compared against the fixture by
# value, so keeping both in one line ending keeps the failure modes to real ones.
# -diff because it is one 8.5 MB line: a retrain would otherwise land in review as a diff no
# tool will render and no human will read. linguist-generated keeps it out of the language
# statistics, where it would otherwise make this a JSON project.
docs/app/model.json text eol=lf -diff linguist-generated
tests/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
# The same distortion as the line above, from a file that is ours rather than generated:
# `01_eda_and_model.ipynb` is 259 433 B against 207 665 B of Python, and GitHub therefore
# reports the repository card as a Jupyter Notebook project — one notebook outweighing the
# package, the API, the site builder and the tests together. `linguist-documentation` and not
# `linguist-vendored`: the notebook is not third-party code, it is the exploratory pass that
# produced the model the API serves, and it stays in the repository, in the diff, and in the
# README. Only the language bar changes.
notebooks/*.ipynb linguist-documentation
